Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.36,0:00:07.48,Newman-CN-4K,,0,0,0,,{\blur10\fad(200,0)}翻译/压制/字幕制作：HAF半个水果
Dialogue: 1,0:00:07.50,0:00:12.70,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}这个名为 homework.mp4 的视频文件几乎有 8 PB 大 
Dialogue: 2,0:00:07.50,0:00:12.70,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}This video file called homework.mp4 is almost 8 petabytes long.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.26,0:00:19.26,Newman-CN-4K,,0,0,0,,{\blur10\fad(200,200)\pos(1936,1874.666)}已获得翻译授权 使用AI工具翻译，如有不准确的地方请在弹幕或评论区指正，谢谢！
Dialogue: 1,0:00:13.24,0:00:14.74,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}我无法正常打开它 
Dialogue: 2,0:00:13.24,0:00:14.74,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}I cannot open it normally,
Dialogue: 1,0:00:15.20,0:00:16.60,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}也无法将其删除 
Dialogue: 2,0:00:15.20,0:00:16.60,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}nor can I recycle it.
Dialogue: 1,0:00:16.86,0:00:18.66,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}它实在是太大了 
Dialogue: 2,0:00:16.86,0:00:18.66,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}It's simply too large.
Dialogue: 1,0:00:19.54,0:00:21.76,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}8 PB 可不是开玩笑的 
Dialogue: 2,0:00:19.54,0:00:21.76,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}8 petabytes is not a joke.
Dialogue: 1,0:00:22.44,0:00:25.26,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}那是 8192 TB 
Dialogue: 2,0:00:22.44,0:00:25.26,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}It's 8192 terabytes.
Dialogue: 1,0:00:26.14,0:00:28.18,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}难道我碰巧拥有一个数据中心？
Dialogue: 2,0:00:26.14,0:00:28.18,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}Do I own a data center by any chance?
Dialogue: 1,0:00:28.58,0:00:29.24,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}不 
Dialogue: 2,0:00:28.58,0:00:29.24,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}No.
Dialogue: 1,0:00:29.76,0:00:32.70,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}我只有一块 512 GB 的硬盘 
Dialogue: 2,0:00:29.76,0:00:32.70,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}I only have a 512 gigabyte disk,
Dialogue: 1,0:00:33.06,0:00:34.78,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}而且它还没被填满
Dialogue: 2,0:00:33.06,0:00:34.78,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}which isn't filled
Dialogue: 1,0:00:35.50,0:00:36.46,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}这到底是怎么回事？
Dialogue: 2,0:00:35.50,0:00:36.46,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}What's the catch?
Dialogue: 1,0:00:38.50,0:00:41.80,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}具体来说是它那漂亮的 NTFS 文件系统 
Dialogue: 2,0:00:38.50,0:00:41.80,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}And specifically its beautiful NTFS file system.
Dialogue: 1,0:00:42.78,0:00:45.52,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}这个 homework 视频并非普通的文件 
Dialogue: 2,0:00:42.78,0:00:45.52,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}The homework video is not just a normal file.
Dialogue: 1,0:00:46.02,0:00:47.58,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}它是一个稀疏文件 
Dialogue: 2,0:00:46.02,0:00:47.58,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}It is a sparse file.
Dialogue: 1,0:00:48.26,0:00:50.72,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}而且这也不是标准的 Windows
Dialogue: 2,0:00:48.26,0:00:50.72,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}And this is not a standard Windows install either.
Dialogue: 1,0:00:51.40,0:00:53.28,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}它占用了惊人的空间 
Dialogue: 2,0:00:51.40,0:00:53.28,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}It takes a surprising amount of space.
Dialogue: 1,0:00:53.69,0:00:55.98,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}377 GB 的数据 
Dialogue: 2,0:00:53.69,0:00:55.98,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}377 gigabytes of data.
Dialogue: 1,0:00:56.72,0:00:59.06,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}你可能会觉得这膨胀得厉害 
Dialogue: 2,0:00:56.72,0:00:59.06,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}And it might sound heavily inflated to you,
Dialogue: 1,0:00:59.14,0:01:00.92,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}这完全正确 
Dialogue: 2,0:00:59.14,0:01:00.92,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}which is a completely right call.
Dialogue: 1,0:01:01.70,0:01:04.82,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}普通干净的 Windows 大约占用 20 GB 存储空间 
Dialogue: 2,0:01:01.70,0:01:04.82,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}A regular clean Windows install takes around 20 gigs of storage.
Dialogue: 1,0:01:05.70,0:01:07.44,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}你可能会问这是为什么？
Dialogue: 2,0:01:05.70,0:01:07.44,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}Why is that, you might ask?
Dialogue: 1,0:01:08.08,0:01:10.10,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0\pos(605.333,2042.667)}原因在于簇大小 
Dialogue: 2,0:01:08.08,0:01:10.10,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0\pos(605.333,2097.667)}The reason for that is cluster size.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.14,0:01:34.69,Enderman-CN-C,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}{\c&H000000&\fscx3336\fscy1624\pos(3072,1546.334)}▮
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.14,0:01:34.69,Enderman-CN-C,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}{\c&H000000&\fscx3626\fscy542\pos(2914.667,1874.335)}▮
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.14,0:01:34.69,Enderman-CN-C,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}{\c&H000000&\fscx3454\fscy207\pos(2877.334,1997)}▮
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.14,0:01:34.69,Enderman-CN-C,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}{\c&H000000&\\fscx3454\fscy207\pos(2896.001,370.333)}▮
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.14,0:01:34.69,Enderman-CN-C,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}{\pos(2898.667,325)}机械硬盘层级
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.14,0:01:34.69,Enderman-CN-C,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}{\pos(2445.333,469)}磁道*
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.14,0:01:34.69,Enderman-CN-C,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)\pos(2426.666,578.332)}{\pos(2442.666,580.999)}扇区
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.14,0:01:34.69,Enderman-CN-C,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}{\pos(2557.333,695.666)}磁道的扇区*
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.14,0:01:34.69,Enderman-CN-C,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)\pos(2424,810.333)}{\pos(2445.333,807.666)}簇**
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.14,0:01:34.69,Enderman-CN-C,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)\pos(2685.333,922.333)}{\pos(2698.666,922.333)}主文件表（文件 0）
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.14,0:01:34.69,Enderman-CN-C,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)\pos(2511.999,1036.999)}{\pos(2519.999,1036.999)}随机文件
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.14,0:01:34.69,Enderman-CN-C,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)\pos(2752,1159.665)}{\pos(2760,1159.665)}F 的 MFT 条目（1KB）
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.14,0:01:34.69,Enderman-CN-C,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)\pos(2741.333,1263.665)}{\pos(2749.333,1268.998)}空白对齐空间（1MB）
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.14,0:01:34.69,Enderman-CN-C,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)\pos(2477.333,1378.332)}{\pos(2520,1386.332)}簇大小
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.14,0:01:34.69,Enderman-CN-C,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}{\pos(2925.333,1796.999)}* 磁道只是早期采用区段位记录技术后消失的抽象概念\N实际上SSD使用的是单元、页和块。\N扇区仍然作为一种抽象概念被使用
Dialogue: 0,0:01:12.14,0:01:34.69,Enderman-CN-C,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)}{\pos(2983.999,1959.665)}**簇纯粹是文件系统抽象，与物理介质类型无关
Dialogue: 1,0:01:10.72,0:01:12.56,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0\pos(754.667,2021.333)}这是文件系统的一个经典属性 
Dialogue: 2,0:01:10.72,0:01:12.56,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0\pos(754.667,2076.333)}That's a classic file system property.
Dialogue: 1,0:01:13.34,0:01:16.12,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0\pos(786.667,2018.667)}簇是卷上分配的基本单位 
Dialogue: 2,0:01:13.34,0:01:16.12,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0\pos(786.667,2073.667)}A cluster is the unit of allocation on a volume.
Dialogue: 1,0:01:17.06,0:01:18.64,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0\pos(576,2002.667)}注意它与文件不同 
Dialogue: 2,0:01:17.06,0:01:18.64,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0\pos(576,2057.667)}Notice it's different from files.
Dialogue: 1,0:01:18.80,0:01:20.36,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0\pos(528,1989.333)}文件本质上是记录 
Dialogue: 2,0:01:18.80,0:01:20.36,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0\pos(528,2044.333)}Files are basically records,
Dialogue: 1,0:01:20.60,0:01:22.52,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0\pos(605.333,1992)}它们位于簇内 
Dialogue: 2,0:01:20.60,0:01:22.52,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0\pos(605.333,2047)}and they're located within clusters.
Dialogue: 1,0:01:23.36,0:01:26.70,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0\pos(970.667,2032)}可以把簇看作磁盘物理表面的标签 
Dialogue: 2,0:01:23.36,0:01:26.70,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0\pos(970.667,2087)}Think of clusters as labels for physical surface on your disk.
Dialogue: 1,0:01:27.60,0:01:31.61,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0\pos(1162.666,2024)}文件并不保证是连续的簇 所以会碎片化 
Dialogue: 2,0:01:27.60,0:01:31.61,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0\pos(1162.666,2079)}Files are not guaranteed consecutive clusters, which causes fragmentation,
Dialogue: 1,0:01:31.96,0:01:34.02,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0\pos(1098.667,2032)}这就是为什么需要在机械硬盘上进行碎片整理 
Dialogue: 2,0:01:31.96,0:01:34.02,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0\pos(1098.667,2087)}that you need to defrag on HDDs.
Dialogue: 1,0:01:34.48,0:01:35.38,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}这真的很简单 
Dialogue: 2,0:01:34.48,0:01:35.38,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}It's really simple.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:35.29,0:01:45.63,Enderman-CN-C,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)\pos(2010.667,1743.667)}想象一下，文件碎片分布在中心附近的簇和相反方向的边缘簇中。那真糟糕！
Dialogue: 1,0:01:35.88,0:01:38.94,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0\pos(1922.667,2069.333)}顺序读取数据远比随机读取要好得多
Dialogue: 2,0:01:35.88,0:01:38.94,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0\pos(1922.667,2124.333)}Sequential data reads are so much better than random reads,
Dialogue: 1,0:01:39.28,0:01:41.56,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0\pos(1917.333,2064)}这在硬盘的物理特性上是直观可见的 
Dialogue: 2,0:01:39.28,0:01:41.56,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0\pos(1917.333,2119)}which is physically intuitive on hard drives.
Dialogue: 1,0:01:42.12,0:01:45.14,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0\pos(1917.333,2080)}磁头移动更少 因为扇区彼此相邻 
Dialogue: 2,0:01:42.12,0:01:45.14,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0\pos(1917.333,2135)}The head moves less because the sectors are next to each other.
Dialogue: 1,0:01:45.74,0:01:49.38,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}因此 簇大小控制着每个物理单元的大小 
Dialogue: 2,0:01:45.74,0:01:49.38,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}So the cluster size controls how large each physical unit is.
Dialogue: 1,0:01:50.00,0:01:52.26,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}由于文件使用这些物理单元 
Dialogue: 2,0:01:50.00,0:01:52.26,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}Since files use those physical units,
Dialogue: 1,0:01:52.48,0:02:00.56,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0\fs130}文件系统中的每个文件至少与一个簇大小相同 但小于约700到800字节的文件除外
Dialogue: 2,0:01:52.48,0:02:00.56,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}each file in the file system is at least the size of a cluster with an exception to files less than around 700 to 800 bytes,
Dialogue: 1,0:02:00.74,0:02:05.28,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}因为主文件表记录设计占用1KB
Dialogue: 2,0:02:00.74,0:02:05.28,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0} due to the master file table record taking up 1 kilobyte by design.
Dialogue: 1,0:02:05.86,0:02:10.36,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}这种臃肿的体积主要源于所谓的闲置空间 
Dialogue: 2,0:02:05.86,0:02:10.36,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}That inflated install size is primarily caused by the so-called slack space,
Dialogue: 1,0:02:10.82,0:02:14.26,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}即文件无法完全放入主文件表的记录中 
Dialogue: 2,0:02:10.82,0:02:14.26,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}where the file cannot fit inside the record in the master file table,
Dialogue: 1,0:02:14.88,0:02:16.80,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}但又不能完全占满整个簇 
Dialogue: 2,0:02:14.88,0:02:16.80,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}but doesn't occupy the cluster entirely.
Dialogue: 1,0:02:17.46,0:02:19.96,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}在我的情况下 簇大小为2MB
Dialogue: 2,0:02:17.46,0:02:19.96,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}In my case, the cluster size is 2 megabytes,
Dialogue: 1,0:02:20.16,0:02:21.90,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}既令人作呕又达到最优 
Dialogue: 2,0:02:20.16,0:02:21.90,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}which is disgusting and optimal.
Dialogue: 1,0:02:22.52,0:02:25.64,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}顺便说一句 这是NTFS的最大簇大小 
Dialogue: 2,0:02:22.52,0:02:25.64,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}And incidentally, the maximum cluster size for NTFS.
Dialogue: 1,0:02:26.58,0:02:29.58,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}我不得不把簇设得如此笨拙可怕 
Dialogue: 2,0:02:26.58,0:02:29.58,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}The only reason I had to make clusters so clunky and horrible,
Dialogue: 1,0:02:30.14,0:02:33.22,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}唯一原因就是要针对文件大小进行优化 
Dialogue: 2,0:02:30.14,0:02:33.22,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}is because it's the only way to optimize for file size.
Dialogue: 1,0:02:34.20,0:02:36.88,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}Windows针对4KB簇进行了优化 
Dialogue: 2,0:02:34.20,0:02:36.88,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}Windows is optimized for 4 kilobyte clusters,
Dialogue: 1,0:02:37.38,0:02:39.82,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}这与内存页对齐得非常好 
Dialogue: 2,0:02:37.38,0:02:39.82,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}which aligns super well with memory pages,
Dialogue: 1,0:02:40.22,0:02:43.69,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}在Windows上这些内存页也都是4KB长 
Dialogue: 2,0:02:40.22,0:02:43.69,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}which are also 4 kilobytes long on Windows.
Dialogue: 1,0:02:43.98,0:02:48.04,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}压缩也仅在簇大小不超过4KB时才能正常工作 这是出于设计的考虑 
Dialogue: 2,0:02:43.98,0:02:48.04,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}Compression also only works with clusters 4 kilobytes and smaller by design.
Dialogue: 1,0:02:48.72,0:02:50.08,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}这完全说得通 
Dialogue: 2,0:02:48.72,0:02:50.08,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}It just totally makes sense.
Dialogue: 1,0:02:50.58,0:02:56.82,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}唯一的问题在于 Windows上的NTFS驱动程序将每个文件的簇数量限制在32位以内 
Dialogue: 2,0:02:50.58,0:02:56.82,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}The only problem is that the NTFS driver on Windows locks the amount of clusters per file to 32 bits,
Dialogue: 1,0:02:57.34,0:03:01.72,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}也就是大约40亿个地址 而NTFS实际上支持64位 
Dialogue: 2,0:02:57.34,0:03:01.72,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}or around 4 billion, while NTFS is actually 64-bit capable.
Dialogue: 1,0:03:02.54,0:03:08.90,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0\fs130}这是由愚蠢的驱动程序导致的缺点 它在普通Windows上强制每个文件16TB的限制 
Dialogue: 2,0:03:02.54,0:03:08.90,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}That is a drawback caused by a stupid driver forcing the 16 terabyte limit per file on a regular Windows install.
Dialogue: 1,0:03:09.58,0:03:14.46,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}提高限制的唯一方法是增加NTFS簇大小 
Dialogue: 2,0:03:09.58,0:03:14.46,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}The only way to increase the limit is by increasing the NTFS cluster size,
Dialogue: 1,0:03:14.46,0:03:16.10,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}这完全是一种权宜之计 
Dialogue: 2,0:03:14.46,0:03:16.10,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}which is a complete hack.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:16.08,0:03:26.38,Enderman-CN-C,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)\pos(1946.667,1749)}我的想法是为什么使用32位簇大小限制来限制文件：驱动程序可能错误地复用了卷大小的常量
Dialogue: 1,0:03:16.48,0:03:20.20,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0\pos(1925.333,1610.667)}使用正确实现NTFS的驱动程序时 你就不需要那样做了 
Dialogue: 2,0:03:16.48,0:03:20.20,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0\pos(1925.333,1665.667)}You won't need to do that with a driver properly implementing NTFS.
Dialogue: 1,0:03:20.78,0:03:21.94,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0\pos(1928,1602.667)}微软在这里失败了 
Dialogue: 2,0:03:20.78,0:03:21.94,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0\pos(1928,1657.667)}Microsoft failed here.
Dialogue: 1,0:03:23.62,0:03:29.80,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0\move(1925.333,1578.667,1925.333,2010.667,2680,3330)}所以Windows理论上最大的文件大小为8PB减去2MB 
Dialogue: 2,0:03:23.62,0:03:29.80,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0\move(1925.333,1633.667,1925.333,2071,2680,3330)}So on Windows, the largest theoretical file is 8 petabytes minus 2 megabytes long.
Dialogue: 1,0:03:30.62,0:03:35.18,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}也就是2的32次方减1乘以2MB
Dialogue: 2,0:03:30.62,0:03:35.18,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}That is 2 to the power of 32 minus 1 times 2 megabytes.
Dialogue: 1,0:03:35.80,0:03:39.08,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}这全是理论 但可以在实践中证明 
Dialogue: 2,0:03:35.80,0:03:39.08,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}It's all theory, but can be proven in practice.
Dialogue: 1,0:03:39.94,0:03:42.64,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}而稀疏文件将帮助我们证明这个限制 
Dialogue: 2,0:03:39.94,0:03:42.64,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}And the sparse files will help us prove the limit.
Dialogue: 1,0:03:43.20,0:03:48.00,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}稀疏文件是NTFS的一个功能 但很大程度上不被Windows用户所认识 
Dialogue: 2,0:03:43.20,0:03:48.00,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}Sparse files are a feature of NTFS and go largely unrecognized by Windows users,
Dialogue: 1,0:03:48.52,0:03:49.58,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}尽管它非常强大 
Dialogue: 2,0:03:48.52,0:03:49.58,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}though really powerful.
Dialogue: 1,0:03:50.58,0:03:52.28,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}它们有助于存储稀疏数据 
Dialogue: 2,0:03:50.58,0:03:52.28,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}They help store sparse data,
Dialogue: 1,0:03:53.00,0:03:56.60,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}即特意在数据之间存储大量零的数据 
Dialogue: 2,0:03:53.00,0:03:56.60,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}or data which is purposefully stored with a lot of zeros in between.
Dialogue: 1,0:03:57.36,0:04:01.23,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}这些零可以被挤掉 有点像被压缩了
Dialogue: 2,0:03:57.36,0:04:01.23,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}Those zeros can be squished, kinda like compressed.
Dialogue: 1,0:04:01.50,0:04:05.72,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}这些对于没有完全分配存储空间的虚拟磁盘来说非常有用 
Dialogue: 2,0:04:01.50,0:04:05.72,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}Those are just nice to have for your virtual disks that aren't fully allocated in storage,
Dialogue: 1,0:04:06.42,0:04:08.64,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}不过例如VMware并没有使用这个功能 
Dialogue: 2,0:04:06.42,0:04:08.64,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}though for example VMware does not use that,
Dialogue: 1,0:04:09.14,0:04:12.72,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}因为VMDK格式自己实现了稀疏性 
Dialogue: 2,0:04:09.14,0:04:12.72,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}because the VMDK format implements sparseness on its own.
Dialogue: 1,0:04:13.92,0:04:16.82,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}我们可以使用fsutil来创建稀疏文件 
Dialogue: 2,0:04:13.92,0:04:16.82,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}We can use fsutil to create sparse files.
Dialogue: 1,0:04:17.34,0:04:18.50,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}这个工具包含在Windows系统中 
Dialogue: 2,0:04:17.34,0:04:18.50,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}It's included in Windows.
Dialogue: 1,0:04:19.18,0:04:20.74,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}首先设置稀疏标记 
Dialogue: 2,0:04:19.18,0:04:20.74,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}First set the sparse flag,
Dialogue: 1,0:04:21.14,0:04:22.58,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}然后设置文件结束位置 
Dialogue: 2,0:04:21.14,0:04:22.58,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}then set the end of file,
Dialogue: 1,0:04:23.10,0:04:23.80,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}再设置范围 
Dialogue: 2,0:04:23.10,0:04:23.80,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}then the range.
Dialogue: 1,0:04:24.38,0:04:25.06,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}这样就完成了 
Dialogue: 2,0:04:24.38,0:04:25.06,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}And that's it.
Dialogue: 1,0:04:25.52,0:04:28.62,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}现在你也拥有一个空的8PB文件 
Dialogue: 2,0:04:25.52,0:04:28.62,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}Now you also own an empty 8 petabyte file.
Dialogue: 1,0:04:29.16,0:04:32.66,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}对于你们所有人来说 如果在自己机器上尝试 大概是16TB左右 
Dialogue: 2,0:04:29.16,0:04:32.66,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}For all of you, it'll be around 16 terabytes if you try it on your machine,
Dialogue: 1,0:04:32.66,0:04:35.50,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}因为优化后的簇大小是4KB 
Dialogue: 2,0:04:32.66,0:04:35.50,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}because of the 4 kilobyte optimized cluster size.
Dialogue: 1,0:04:36.12,0:04:40.09,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}理论上 你可以达到16EB减去1KB
Dialogue: 2,0:04:36.12,0:04:40.09,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}In theory, you can reach 16 exabytes minus a kilobyte.
Dialogue: 1,0:04:40.40,0:04:42.34,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}这就是NTFS的限制 
Dialogue: 2,0:04:40.40,0:04:42.34,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}That's the NTFS limitation.
Dialogue: 1,0:04:43.12,0:04:45.88,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}不过在Windows上 大约是8PB
Dialogue: 2,0:04:43.12,0:04:45.88,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}On Windows, though, it's around 8 petabytes,
Dialogue: 1,0:04:46.16,0:04:50.04,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}就像这里展示的 而且只有在你使用未优化的设置时才能实现 
Dialogue: 2,0:04:46.16,0:04:50.04,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}as shown here, and only if you go for an unoptimized setup,
Dialogue: 1,0:04:50.22,0:04:52.54,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}而这种设置甚至无法通过常规方式安装 
Dialogue: 2,0:04:50.22,0:04:52.54,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}which you can't even install through normal means.
Dialogue: 1,0:04:53.38,0:04:56.20,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}这就是我在NTFS上获得最大文件的方法 
Dialogue: 2,0:04:53.38,0:04:56.20,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}So that's how I got my largest file on NTFS.
Dialogue: 1,0:04:56.20,0:04:57.78,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}感谢观看 
Dialogue: 2,0:04:56.20,0:04:57.78,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}Thank you for watching,
Dialogue: 1,0:04:58.20,0:04:58.86,Enderman字幕中,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}保重！
Dialogue: 2,0:04:58.20,0:04:58.86,Enderman字幕英,,0,0,0,,{\blur15.0}and take care!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.68,0:05:19.39,Newman-CN-4K,,0,0,0,,{\fad(200,200)\blur30\fscx151\fscy153\pos(1944,742.666)}在 Youtube 上关注
